      "problem": "Find the derivative of $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-11.$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-11) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
